# Content Authoring Guidelines

## Frontmatter Schema
```yaml
---
title: "Your Title Here"
date: 2026-04-19          # ISO 8601, required
description: "One sentence — used in listings and meta description"
tags: [tag1, tag2]        # optional
draft: false              # true = excluded from build and deploy
lang: en                  # optional: en (default) or pl
---
```
`date`, `title`, `description`, and `draft` are required by the Zod schema in `src/content/config.ts`.

## Blog Posts (`src/content/blog/`)
- Short, focused entries (300–1500 words)
- Filename becomes the URL slug: `2026-04-19-my-post.md` → `/blog/2026-04-19-my-post`
- Conversational but professional tone
- Can be in Polish or English — use `lang: pl` for Polish posts

## Articles (`src/content/articles/`)
- Long-form, technical or professional content (1500+ words)
- Filename = topic slug: `how-this-site-is-built.md` → `/articles/how-this-site-is-built`
- Use `##` and `###` headings to structure for navigation
- Code blocks must include a language: ` ```typescript ` not ` ``` `

## Markdown Conventions
- **No `# H1` in the body** — the title comes from frontmatter and is rendered by the layout
- Start body content from `##` sections or plain paragraphs
- External links: prefer reference-style at the bottom of the file
- Images: place in `src/assets/`, reference with relative path:
  ```md
  ![alt text](../../assets/my-image.jpg)
  ```
  Astro will optimize these at build time via `<Image>`.

## Publishing Checklist
- [ ] `draft: false`
- [ ] `date` is correct (ISO 8601)
- [ ] `description` is one clear sentence
- [ ] No `# H1` in the body
- [ ] Committed and pushed to `main`
